Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.60,0:00:09.82,Default,Young,0,0,0,,This sucks! This is the worst day ever!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.82,0:00:13.11,Default,Veteran,0,0,0,,If you've got time to bitch, \Nyou could be running faster!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.11,0:00:15.83,Default,Young,0,0,0,,What good is running even gonna do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.83,0:00:19.99,Default,Veteran,0,0,0,,If we keep running 'til we're out of \Nthis forest, we can contact the guild!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.99,0:00:21.50,Default,Young,0,0,0,,Again!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.90,0:00:24.04,Default,Young,0,0,0,,What good would that even do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.04,0:00:25.18,Default,Young,0,0,0,,That thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.66,0:00:26.83,Default,Young,0,0,0,,That thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.12,0:00:35.54,Default,Young,0,0,0,,It'll wipe out more than just the town.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.42,0:00:38.50,Default,Young,0,0,0,,It'll destroy the entire kingdom!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.55,0:02:10.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:02:02.55,0:02:10.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.55,0:02:10.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.48,0:02:27.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was out for a while...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.05,0:02:29.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry about that. \NThanks for lending me your lap.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.91,0:02:34.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Not at all. I'm just glad \NI could be somewhat useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.06,0:02:43.26,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.53,0:02:46.44,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You mustn't doze off outside like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.27,0:02:48.85,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You caught me, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.85,0:02:52.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie's lap was just so comfy to sleep on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.05,0:02:56.82,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Honestly, Princess, you so readily leave \Nyourself vulnerable to the person you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.82,0:02:58.15,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Just like a dog—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.42,0:02:59.23,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.23,0:03:03.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ilia, were you about to say \Nsomething super disrespectful?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.21,0:03:05.16,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Most certainly not.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.16,0:03:10.28,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I merely thought that even a stray dog would \Ndevote more attention to personal grooming.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.99,0:03:14.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,D-Disrespect! Disrespect! No tact at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.40,0:03:20.06,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Incidentally, your odor was so foul that \Na stray dog would whimper and run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.80,0:03:23.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Disrespect! Disrespect! \NAnd even more unnecessary!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.14,0:03:27.31,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Your hair is a mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.75,0:03:31.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Thanks, Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.19,0:03:35.08,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If you can't even handle this by yourself, \Na dog really would be better.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.04,0:03:40.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.36,0:03:48.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hey, Euphie...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.25,0:03:50.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.66,0:03:59.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think it might be a cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.01,0:04:01.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, no, it's nothing like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.38,0:04:05.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you okay? You don't feel \Nchilled, or weak, or achy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.88,0:04:07.48,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm fine, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.47,0:04:10.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Maybe you were in the outside air too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.94,0:04:12.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.19,0:04:15.20,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, really, it's nothing serious...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.20,0:04:17.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, it's too late to do \Nanything once it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.81,0:04:19.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sit tight! I'll get you some medicine!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.81,0:04:21.45,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ah... Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.42,0:04:31.24,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What am I doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.77,0:04:38.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm back, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.74,0:04:41.20,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Th-That certainly was quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.54,0:04:44.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I guess we can at least get \Nsome medicine in you for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.93,0:04:48.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Try to ignore how bitter it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.62,0:04:50.47,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.06,0:04:56.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You got it all down! Good girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.90,0:05:00.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis... I'm not a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.17,0:05:04.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry, couldn't help myself. \NI {\i1}am{\i0} an older sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.99,0:05:08.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I think it's probably fatigue. \NYou can just take it easy, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.90,0:05:12.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to put you \Nthrough all this trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.19,0:05:15.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's not a problem. Just rest up.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.85,0:05:25.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I think I got so wrapped up \Nin making Arc-en-Ciel
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.16,0:05:28.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that I wasn't paying \Nenough attention to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.83,0:05:32.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, but Arc-en-Ciel \Nreally is amazing, though!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.47,0:05:35.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I love how it came out! It's even better \Nthan last year's masterpiece,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.35,0:05:37.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,which they called the best in a decade!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.73,0:05:39.28,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's elegant and profound enough
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.28,0:05:41.97,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,to be comparable to the legendary \Nmagic tool of the year before!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.97,0:05:44.62,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's why I want you to get \Nplenty of rest now
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.97,0:05:47.14,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis is like a beautiful bird \Nthat flies as far as it wants.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.62,0:05:48.96,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so you'll be in top form to use Arc-en-Ciel \Nbeautifully and masterfully!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.12,0:05:53.36,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But I...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.47,0:05:57.24,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,will never go anywhere. I just keep falling.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.61,0:06:03.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm empty...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.10,0:06:06.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.63,0:06:11.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.25,0:06:20.54,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I envy you, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.81,0:06:21.65,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.93,0:06:24.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I have nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.82,0:06:28.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Nothing at all, unlike you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.38,0:06:34.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You really are such an awkward girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.18,0:06:38.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.96,0:06:44.58,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What shall I do from here on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.12,0:06:46.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Good question...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.48,0:06:50.55,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I think you should do what you want to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.66,0:06:53.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And if I don't know what that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.21,0:06:58.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I want you to give me an order.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.26,0:07:00.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,An order?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.05,0:07:06.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If it is your wish as one of the royal \Nfamily, I know I can do it, whatever it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.83,0:07:10.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.78,0:07:18.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you don't know what you want, \Nor what you {\i1}should{\i0} want,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.78,0:07:21.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,we can take our time \Nlooking for it together.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.42,0:07:24.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Together?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.42,0:07:29.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm happy just having you here \Nto laugh with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.19,0:07:31.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm going to set you free.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.63,0:07:33.84,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.53,0:07:37.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But you gotta get better first.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.80,0:07:40.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just stay there and don't move, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.27,0:07:41.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,H-Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.72,0:07:43.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come on, hold still.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.64,0:07:44.99,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What are you—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.31,0:07:46.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wh...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.26,0:07:48.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Ani—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.73,0:08:08.60,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis's warmth feels so nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.87,0:08:16.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, I still think you're a bit feverish.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.33,0:08:20.17,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, I'm just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.89,0:08:26.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come on, time to sleep. \NI'll sing you a lullaby!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.01,0:08:27.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,There's no need for that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.60,0:08:43.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, you'll catch a cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.31,0:08:46.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Honestly...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.79,0:08:51.90,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You shine too brightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.06,0:08:56.42,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You feel so warm, it makes my chest ache...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.26,0:08:59.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and I don't think I can ever let go now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.68,0:09:11.49,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.63,0:09:14.30,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Pardon me, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.28,0:09:18.65,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,An inept prince under house arrest, \Nand the head of the Ministry of the Arcane...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.29,0:09:22.06,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Should we not refrain \Nfrom unnecessary contact?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.78,0:09:26.58,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Well, the truth is, \Nthe situation has changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.48,0:09:28.47,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,The situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.33,0:09:34.86,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,This is the perfect opportunity to be \Nfreed of your meaningless house arrest.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.95,0:09:50.71,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I feel much lighter than I did yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.29,0:09:54.69,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Maybe it's because I got some rest... or...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.23,0:10:01.84,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.14,0:10:11.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Form refinement training?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.22,0:10:15.08,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The princess's forms are self-taught.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.80,0:10:17.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ilia...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.85,0:10:22.08,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She's been trained by the royal \Nknights in the fundamentals,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.08,0:10:25.04,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,but most of her skills \Nhave been honed in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.93,0:10:27.11,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,In battle?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.11,0:10:30.77,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,More importantly, Lady Euphyllia, \Nhow are you feeling?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.77,0:10:34.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh... I feel much better now, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.96,0:10:36.91,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I'm glad to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.32,0:10:41.55,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Perhaps the change in environment, \Nand in your mentality, took a toll on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.21,0:10:45.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm grateful to both of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.81,0:10:47.79,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You honor me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.79,0:10:50.10,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Please do take care of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.47,0:11:05.36,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I sort of followed her because \NI have nothing else to do...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.13,0:11:07.32,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,May I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.32,0:11:09.40,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Uh, no, I'm fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.40,0:11:10.52,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.30,0:11:19.83,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You need not help me if you \Nfeel uncomfortable doing so.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.19,0:11:25.62,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Do you find it difficult to voluntarily \Ndo things outside your given role?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.69,0:11:30.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That face says I've hit the nail on the head.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.93,0:11:34.65,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.16,0:11:38.12,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ever since I was young, \NI have devoted my efforts
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.12,0:11:42.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,to being a future queen and duke's daughter \Nwho would bring no shame upon the family.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.01,0:11:43.88,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.63,0:11:49.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I believed that was who \Neveryone wanted me to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.04,0:11:53.42,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,So you thought being the ideal \Nthat everyone wanted you to be
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.42,0:11:56.43,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,was what determined your worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.33,0:12:01.29,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can't deny that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.18,0:12:15.19,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Perhaps it's simply the princess's \Nhobby to ensnare such people.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.72,0:12:21.42,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The relationship you share with Miss Anis \Nis... well... rather unusual, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.85,0:12:25.63,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Well, the princess hates being treated \Nwith the esteem of royalty,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.99,0:12:28.49,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,so I play along with her silliness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.49,0:12:33.11,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,From the bottom of my heart, I would love \Nto treat her with due respect, but alas...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.40,0:12:36.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No one else could handle her \Nthat way but you, Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.18,0:12:41.26,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I was once someone who simply \Nfit into a mold, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.48,0:12:45.27,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I never defied what my parents said.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.27,0:12:48.17,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Even when they ordered me \Nto marry an old, rich man,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.17,0:12:50.94,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I did not question them in the least.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.94,0:12:54.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Is that... what you'd call \Nfitting into a mold?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.39,0:12:56.68,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.13,0:12:59.64,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The well-molded life I lived
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.64,0:13:03.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,was quite soundly shattered by a \Ncertain mold-breaking princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.55,0:13:05.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.09,0:13:08.81,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Now, all I want to say to my parents...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.02,0:13:13.27,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,is that they deserve whatever \Nmay be coming to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.38,0:13:19.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You have become quite the, um... \Nunique character, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.32,0:13:23.04,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You honor me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:24.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That wasn't a compliment...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.80,0:13:26.92,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,And that is why...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.66,0:13:31.61,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I can't seem to leave you alone, \Nfor reasons that differ from the princess's.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.94,0:13:33.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.19,0:13:37.58,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia, you are \Na very reasonable person.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.08,0:13:40.54,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That eccentric princess aside,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.54,0:13:43.60,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I'm sure you were much less of \Na handful than I was back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.06,0:13:46.08,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I can guarantee it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.31,0:13:50.72,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,And that is exactly why you \Nhave every right to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.20,0:13:53.87,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,So please worry to your heart's content.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.22,0:13:59.43,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The princess will buy you all \Nthe time you need to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.51,0:14:01.61,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ilia...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.39,0:14:04.75,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Even if it seems like it's too late,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.75,0:14:08.27,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,she'll just say that she'll assume \Nresponsibility and take you in.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.96,0:14:10.59,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Like she did with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.89,0:14:17.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't quite know how to say it yet, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.30,0:14:19.09,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.03,0:14:25.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I believe my coming to this \Nvilla was a good thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.02,0:14:32.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.22,0:14:33.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.94,0:14:36.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huge news!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.33,0:14:42.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's an urgent missive from \Nthe adventurers' guild!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.51,0:14:47.11,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wait, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.57,0:14:53.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why would you receive a summons \Nfrom the adventurers' guild, Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.13,0:14:55.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.30,0:14:59.31,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I {\i1}am{\i0} a high-ranking adventurer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.04,0:15:00.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,G...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.20,0:15:02.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Gold rank?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.42,0:15:07.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But how could a princess be an adventurer?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.20,0:15:10.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, I want materials from monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.99,0:15:13.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,plus it's nice if I can earn \Nfunding for myself, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.89,0:15:16.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You've taken your devotion \Nto your research too far!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.64,0:15:17.44,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.44,0:15:18.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.90,0:15:21.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's urgent this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.68,0:15:22.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,A huge pack of monsters—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.06,0:15:25.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,a stampede—is coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.35,0:15:31.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Do you know what causes stampedes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.00,0:15:34.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Is it when monsters fight over territory?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.43,0:15:39.41,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The losing side has to go \Nlook for a new home,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.41,0:15:41.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,which brings them close \Nto towns and villages.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.55,0:15:45.28,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But there's one other cause.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.28,0:15:46.45,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.21,0:15:51.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,When a monster shows up \Nthat's so big and powerful
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.73,0:15:53.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that it sends whole packs running in fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.59,0:15:58.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So I have to get out there right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.74,0:16:04.52,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why does any of that mean \N{\i1}you{\i0} have to go out there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.96,0:16:10.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Because I know for sure that this stampede \Nwas set off by a magicite monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.95,0:16:15.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,One that I'll never have a chance \Nat again if I miss it this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.01,0:16:18.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The pinnacle of life itself, feared by all...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.29,0:16:20.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,A dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.62,0:16:22.87,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A dragon?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.45,0:16:26.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I want that magicite, whatever it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.69,0:16:30.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What impels you to go to such lengths?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.38,0:16:34.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If I want to continue being me...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.31,0:16:37.97,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I have to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.82,0:16:46.97,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.35,0:16:49.75,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,She is someone...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.51,0:16:55.03,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,who can fly as far as she wants, \Nall by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.94,0:17:00.84,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.23,0:17:06.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.60,0:17:11.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If you insist that you must go,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.84,0:17:13.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,then please take me with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.02,0:17:16.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.04,0:17:20.03,Default,StatesmanB,0,0,0,,Here is our report.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.03,0:17:23.06,Default,StatesmanB,0,0,0,,To counter the dragon and the monster pack,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.06,0:17:27.10,Default,StatesmanB,0,0,0,,the royal knights and the guild are steadily \Nbolstering our defenses on the front li—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.10,0:17:29.50,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Steadily bolstering defense?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.03,0:17:34.03,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I believe you may be misunderstanding \Nthe situation we're in.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.77,0:17:38.01,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Were this a typical stampede,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.01,0:17:40.79,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,building a line of defense \Nwouldn't be wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.14,0:17:44.75,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,But in this case, we're up against a dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.75,0:17:47.45,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Dragons fly, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.45,0:17:51.96,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,No amount of ground defense is any use \Nagainst a calamity from the skies!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.96,0:17:55.60,Default,StatesmanA,0,0,0,,Then shouldn't we avoid provoking it \Nand pray it simply passes by?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.60,0:17:57.94,Default,StatesmanC,0,0,0,,So we just ignore the pack of monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.24,0:18:01.33,Default,StatesmanA,0,0,0,,The dragon might target the pack.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.33,0:18:02.14,Default,StatesmanC,0,0,0,,Surely not...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.97,0:18:06.81,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Monsters attack and eat other monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.81,0:18:11.90,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,There's little doubt that the dragon's \Ncurrent target is the monster pack.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.14,0:18:17.86,Default,StatesmanB,0,0,0,,Which means, if we just focus on any \Nmonsters that stray from the pack...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.26,0:18:22.33,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Then you would be taking the dragon's \Nprey right out from under it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.04,0:18:27.52,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Once the dragon loses its prey, \Nits next target will be...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.97,0:18:28.99,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.25,0:18:34.88,Default,StatesmanA,0,0,0,,We're in danger whether we defend or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.88,0:18:37.96,Default,StatesmanA,0,0,0,,There's no telling if we \Neven {\i1}can{\i0} defend against it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.96,0:18:39.91,Default,StatesmanB,0,0,0,,So what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.91,0:18:43.93,Default,StatesmanC,0,0,0,,This is the first dragon attack \Nin the history of the kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.93,0:18:45.96,Default,StatesmanC,0,0,0,,Nobody knows what to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.11,0:18:49.09,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.09,0:18:50.10,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.37,0:18:51.63,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It's Algard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.50,0:18:59.24,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Forgive me, Father,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.77,0:19:02.72,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,but I heard that a dragon has appeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.28,0:19:06.41,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Just where in the world did you hear that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.41,0:19:09.51,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You're under house arrest. \NWhat business is it of yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.96,0:19:14.72,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I request your permission to participate \Nin the slaying of the dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.34,0:19:18.80,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Just what are you saying?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.20,0:19:22.07,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,There is something I want.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.07,0:19:27.83,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I would like to receive it as a \Nreward for defeating the dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.30,0:19:33.06,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I am prepared to risk my life for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.30,0:19:38.70,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,The daughter of Baron Cyan, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.40,0:19:42.91,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I haven't the time to explain \Nmy feelings to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.48,0:19:44.49,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.77,0:19:48.45,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I cannot simply resign myself to this fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.54,0:19:51.92,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What is that look in his eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.92,0:19:54.14,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,He isn't blinded by love.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.14,0:19:57.15,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,He's simply fallen into obscuring darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.12,0:20:02.89,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,To merely walk down your predetermined \Npath as it was given to you...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.16,0:20:07.09,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Does our kingdom truly need such a king?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.82,0:20:10.30,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What are you trying to say, Algard?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.03,0:20:15.29,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,"If only {\i1}she{\i0} had the \Nability to use magic..."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.72,0:20:18.61,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,"If only {\i1}she{\i0} were a man..."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.20,0:20:23.53,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,When such murmurs are all around me, \Ndo you think I don't hear them?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.45,0:20:36.66,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,When Anisphia and Algard were young, \Nthey were quite close.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.45,0:20:41.09,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,They were always together, \Nlaughing at the same things.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.54,0:20:46.81,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But after Anisphia discovered \Nthe path of magicology,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.81,0:20:49.93,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,something began to go wrong, \Nlittle by little.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.14,0:20:54.46,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,The truth is, I'm well aware...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.77,0:20:57.81,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,that the reason Anisphia \Ngave up her right to the throne
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.81,0:21:02.09,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,and began to behave so foolishly \Nwas for her brother's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.51,0:21:06.29,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,She wanted to make it clear that she didn't \Nhave what it took to assume that role.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.30,0:21:11.28,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But still, someone yet keeps \Nthe rumor alive today...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.27,0:21:15.55,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That Algard has no talent \Nthat makes him shine,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.14,0:21:19.74,DefaultItalics,Orphanse,0,0,0,,and maybe, just maybe, \NAnisphia is the one who...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.28,0:21:27.17,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,As your father, I'll ask you \Njust one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.59,0:21:30.82,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You are certain you're \Nprepared to risk your life?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.82,0:21:33.60,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I'm prepared for everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.28,0:21:37.30,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I see it's inevitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.36,0:21:41.62,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I order you as king, Algard!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.62,0:21:44.49,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Y-Your Majesty! I bring terrible news!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.49,0:21:46.56,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Witnesses have reported \Nthat Princess Anisphia
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.56,0:21:51.90,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,has taken flight toward the Black Forest... \Nwith Lady Euphyllia!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.60,0:22:02.51,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That stupid daughter of mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.50,0:22:05.01,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Four\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Princess and the Lost Child\N Announce Their Decision
